<title>FRANCE: Societe Generale H1 net attrib up 20.9 pct.</title>
<headline>Societe Generale H1 net attrib up 20.9 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>First half 1996.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of French francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net attributable			   2,732  vs	   2,260</p>
<p>    Net					    2,955  vs	   2,416</p>
<p>    Net banking income			21,230  vs	  19,547</p>
<p>    Gross operating profit		   6,174  vs	   5,491</p>
<p>    Operating costs			   15,056  vs	  14,856</p>
<p>    Net new provisions			 2,574  vs	   2,562</p>
<p>    Balance sheet assets (billions)	1,766  vs	 1,623.3</p>
<p>    Customer credits (billions)		682  vs	   653.3</p>
<p>    Customer deposits (billions)	     470  vs	   440.5</p>
<p>    Shareholder funds			   54.7  vs	    49.7</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts polled by Reuters at the start of the bank results reporting season provided a consensus forecast of 2.57 billion francs net attributable profit and a range of 2.3-2.91 billion.</p>
<p>Chairman Marc Vienot said in a July newspaper interview that he expected a &quot;significant rise&quot; in first-half net attributable profit, given capital gains on its industrial portfolio, versus the first half of 1995.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
